From 4839bd2750819eeb4d2c4945b1adbab247031c7e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 1 Jul 2026 23:08:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 05381/11362] [outer-loop] fix systemic map_status_label bug +
 WRONG_MECHANISM_PRECONDITION negation false-positive

Direct follow-up to 'look at the violations first' -- traced .471's stuck
activation loop (43 refusals over 1.5+ hours) past the 3 individual task
problems to a real, project-wide root cause.

MAIN FIX: scripts/in_process_doc_reconcile.py's map_status_label (used by
FailureLedger to decide what counts as a 'prior failure' for doomed-rerun
scope-matching) had ZERO terminal-prefix awareness, unlike its sibling
classifier in research_conductor.py. _WIN_TOKENS never contained 'success'
(only 'ships', not 'shipped'; no 'passed' at all) despite CLAUDE.md's
Verdict Terminal-Prefix Discipline mandating exactly those four prefix
families. Corpus-wide scan (4160 artifacts): 352 success:-prefixed and 13
shipped:-prefixed artifacts were pure-oversight misclassifications (zero
genuine negative content) silently counted as failures. Fixed by adding
success/succeeded/shipped/passed to _WIN_TOKENS. Verified additive-safe:
0 artifacts flipped away from Complete (blocked/failed/partial tokens
still checked first in the cascade); 434 flipped TO Complete, manually
spot-checked -- all genuine wins.

SECOND FIX: WRONG_MECHANISM_PRECONDITION (the pre-existing KV260
/dev/mmcblk check) had no negation awareness -- .471's exp5144 correctly
says 'Do not touch host /dev/mmcblk* for KV260; use SSH to the board' but
got HARD-blocked for containing both the board reference and the retired
path string. Added _is_negated_context (tight character-window negation
check) to exclusion_manifest_lint.py.

Net effect: .471's 4 HARD violations -> 2. The 2 remaining (exp5140
symbolic-KAN, exp5141 HUBO residual-exponent matching this session's own
weak-fit result) are genuine scope-matches needing prior_failures:, not
classifier bugs -- traced and reported, not silently patched.

8 new tests total (5 in test_in_process_doc_reconcile.py, 3 in
test_exclusion_manifest_lint.py), all passing except one confirmed
pre-existing unrelated failure (test_is_doomed_rerun_blocks_recurring_
live_benchmark_chain, already isolated via git-stash comparison earlier
this session).

